<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04KS">Remark <span data-tag="04KS">11.9.2.12</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category which admits pushouts, let $w: X \rightarrow Y$ be a morphism of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, and let $\gamma _{X/Y}: Y \coprod _{X} Y \rightarrow Y$ be the relative codiagonal of $w$. If an object $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $w$-local (in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02FZ" href="/tag/02FZ">6.2.3.1</a>), then it is also $\gamma _{X/Y}$-local. This follows by applying Remark <a data-tag="04KR" href="/tag/04KR">6.2.3.7</a> to the diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  Y \coprod _{X} Y \ar [dr]^{\gamma _{X/Y}} &amp;  \\ Y \ar [ur]^{w'} \ar [rr]^{\operatorname{id}} &amp;  &amp;  Y; } \]
</div>
<p> here $w'$ is a pushout of $w$ (so that $C$ is $w'$-local by virtue of Remark <a data-tag="04KP" href="/tag/04KP">11.9.2.11</a>). </p>
</article>
